1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Water enters concrete through cracks and joints.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,400
Carbon dioxide advances through the cover.

3
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:10,000
At the rebar, corrosion follows, and the surface spalls.

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:13,500
Sun and temperature cycles work on exposed surfaces.

5
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:16,885
A building has seven places that need protection.

6
00:00:16,885 --> 00:00:19,000
Each has its own products.

7
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:19,833
Below ground:

8
00:00:19,833 --> 00:00:21,500
raft, walls, lift pits.

9
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:24,000
Roofs and podium decks.

10
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:26,500
Wet areas and balconies.

11
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:29,000
Water tanks and water-retaining structures.

12
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:31,500
Joints and penetrations.

13
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:34,000
Façades and exposed concrete.

14
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:37,500
Steel and industrial exposure.

